Issue:
User reports inability to log into their account, receiving an “incorrect password” error despite entering valid credentials.

Environment:

Windows domain environment
Standard user account authentication

Troubleshooting Steps Taken:

Confirmed error message and user-reported symptoms
Checked for account lockout status due to multiple failed login attempts
Verified account is active and not disabled or expired
Performed identity verification in accordance with security policy prior to any changes
Reviewed authentication status and reset credentials following standard procedure
Ensured account was configured to require password update at next login (if applicable)

Root Cause:
Account lockout due to multiple failed login attempts or password expiration within authentication system.

Resolution:

Account unlocked through administrative tools
Password reset performed following security verification procedures
User successfully logged in after reset
Login confirmed during live verification session

Tools Used:

Authentication / account management system (e.g., Active Directory conceptually)
Help desk ticketing workflow
Password reset tools
